ts at the same uncertainty ceiling as any other unmeasured category.","`measuredWeight` (0..1, alongside `confidence`) is the share of the category weight that fed the overall score; a reader should trust a headline number in proportion to it, since a low risk built on a small measured slice is not the same claim as a low risk built on all seven.","Scores are trust, not a quality rating: 100 means nothing risky was observed, 0 means the worst observable state. They are never a recommendation.","Scores from the probabilistic layer -- wallet clustering, Sybil and insider grouping, wash-trading likelihood and creator fingerprinting -- are snapped to the nearest 5 before they are scored, so that independent implementations of those heuristics can agree on a value without coordinating on one. Every signal marked probabilistic in this report was rounded that way; the deterministic core was not.","Categories scored at the uncertainty floor in this run: creator."],"scoring":"Each signal contributes points to one risk category internally, weighted by its own confidence; category risk is combined into an overall risk with fixed weights and published as trust, 100 minus that risk. See docs/AUDIT_PROTOCOL.md for the full table.","uncertaintyCeiling":65,"weights":[{"category":"contract","description":"Powers the deployed code grants: minting, pausing, deny-lists, mutable fees, upgradeability, privileged balance movement, and whether source is verified.","weight":0.3},{"category":"liquidity","description":"Depth of the discovered pools on the quote side, and whether the provider position is locked or burned.","weight":0.2},{"category":"holder","description":"Concentration of circulating supply across the sampled holders, with pools, burn addresses and the token contract itself excluded.","weight":0.15},{"category":"insider","description":"Wallets that share a funding source, and transfers that fund several recipients at once.","weight":0.1},{"category":"creator","description":"Th